alc5623: accept a zero sysclk

With mclk-fs, simple-card releases the codec clock on shutdown by setting
sysclk to 0. The driver rejected that, so every stream close logged
"ASoC: error at snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk on alc5621-hifi: -22". The next
hw_params sets the real clock again.

--- a/alc5623.c
+++ b/alc5623.c
@@ -621,6 +621,7 @@
 	struct alc5623_priv *alc5623 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 
 	switch (freq) {
+	case 0:
 	case  8192000:
 	case 11289600:
 	case 12288000:
